cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use rggmci, please cite it as below, and cite antiSMASH, whose output it reads."
title: "rggmci: Reference-Guided Genome Mining Candidate Inference"
abstract: >-
  Surfaces antiSMASH regions in a fragmented genome assembly that may belong to one biosynthetic pathway,
  by reading the ClusterBlast and KnownClusterBlast results antiSMASH already wrote. A candidate is a
  hypothesis to check at gene level, not a joined contig.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Smith
    given-names: Alexander J.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/alexanderjsmith1/rggmci"
version: 1.0.0rc1
references:
  - type: article
    title: "antiSMASH 8.0"
    doi: 10.1093/nar/gkaf334
  - type: article
    title: "MIBiG 4.0"
    doi: 10.1093/nar/gkae1115
